    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460-a1">

                <pb facs="0550" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg470"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dubber to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cleveland, Ohio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Information has reached me that my
                    brother, Dirk J. Dubber, is now a prisoner of war on parole at Pretoria, South
                    African Republic.</p>
                <p>I would hereby kindly ask the good offices of our Government to request the
                    English Government to transport the said D. J. Dubber to some English, or if in
                    order, better still, to some Dutch port, whence I will guarantee payment for his
                    transportation to Cleveland, Ohio.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arie Dubber.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
